From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] winmm: mmioOpen PARSE/EXIST results, mciSendString parser errors, device all, auto-open notify

Groups the conformance tests had marked todo_wine:

- mmioOpen with MMIO_PARSE / MMIO_EXIST: the name buffer is 128 characters
  (MMIOERR_OUTOFMEMORY and a FALSE result when the full path does not fit; the
  wide flavour hands the path back cut to 127 characters, the ansi one leaves the
  name alone), MMIO_EXIST on a missing file sets MMIOERR_FILENOTFOUND, and the
  wide flavour writes the parsed path back to the caller's buffer.
- mciSendString parser: duplicate flags (MCIERR_DUPLICATE_FLAGS), two constants
  of one group (MCIERR_FLAGS_NOT_COMPATIBLE), constants of a named group
  ("time format milliseconds") only after their name, an unknown word is
  MCIERR_BAD_CONSTANT where a constant or number may stand and
  MCIERR_UNRECOGNIZED_KEYWORD elsewhere, a number may be followed by further
  flags ("status x 4 notify"), any run of blanks matches the blank of a
  multi-word keyword ("can   save") and blanks between verb and device are
  skipped; "open notify" is MCIERR_INVALID_DEVICE_NAME, "open new" without an
  alias MCIERR_NEW_REQUIRES_ALIAS, "open all" MCIERR_CANNOT_USE_ALL.
- Device "all": pause, resume and stop go to every open device and give the
  common answer or MCIERR_MULTIPLE; other commands are MCIERR_CANNOT_USE_ALL.
- Auto-open: notify is refused before the device is opened
  (MCIERR_NOTIFY_ON_AUTO_OPEN); a device left open by an auto-opened play or
  record refuses notify as well, is closed by stop and found closed once it
  stopped, as if it had closed itself.
- MMIO_GETTEMP and global IO procs: no documented contract; the FIXMEs became
  warnings (global procs are registered for the process only).

